{%- comment -%}
  TJJM removed-index — the suppressed legacy gym names for every state, one row per state.
  Format: <STATE CODE>|<name>|<name>|...   Read by sections/tjjm-state-directory.liquid,
  the same way tjjm-region-index is read: strip, newline_to_br, split on '<br />'.

  Moved out of the section on 5 Aug 2026 to reclaim section headroom
  (the section was at 20,758 B against the Admin API's ~24 KB rewrite ceiling).

  RULES
  - Removal matches on the EXACT gym name. Before adding a name, check it against the names
    you are KEEPING: legacyNames.filter(n => keptNames.has(n)). A collision deletes BOTH
    records and nothing in the count-based verification catches it, because the counts agree.
  - ALSO CHECK DOMAINS, NOT JUST NAMES. Oregon (5 Aug 2026) found two legacy records that
    shared a domain with a MatMade record under a DIFFERENT name, which the name-only check
    cannot see: legacyDomains ∩ keptDomains. Run both.
  - When a legacy name and a MatMade name collide, do NOT list it here. Keep the legacy
    record, drop the MatMade duplicate, and supply the address via tjjm-gym-addresses.
  - Arizona has NO fakes, so AZ has no row.
  - WA NOTE: "Bellingham BJJ" is deliberately ABSENT from the WA row for exactly that reason.
  - OR NOTE: "Ashland BJJ" is deliberately ABSENT from the OR row for the same reason — it
    shares ashlandbjj.com with MatMade's "Ashland Jiu-jitsu Academy", which was not imported.
  - CA NOTE: "MZ Brazilian Jiu-Jitsu" is a MATMADE record, not a legacy one — the only such
    entry in this file. It is a stale listing of Mendes Jiu-Jitsu HQ: same building on
    Deschutes Rd, same domain (reddingselfdefense.com), and that site lists only Ste 5&7 and
    never mentions MZ. Removal matches on name from either source, so this works.
  - Names must not contain "|" — the section splits on it.
  - Per-state rationale lives in snippets/tjjm-statedir-notes and tjjm-statedir-notes-<code>.
